(440042, 39802, 4493, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo. This is what I feel real photography is all about!</td>', 'Excellent photo. This is what I feel real photography is all about!', '2003-10-06 01:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(440043, 40047, 10167, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for the votes and kind comments left below...<br/> <br/>For those who asked, this was taken with me on the ground, and the plane was just about leveled off from a banked turn as it passed in front of me.  It was taken at Alliance Air Show in Fort Worth Texas, and the shot is of pilot Gene Soucy and his brave wing-walking accomplice, Teresa Stokes.  I had been panning with the plane through its turn and I let the camera track it with its AI Servo focus mode.  I was shooting handheld with a Sigma 50-500mm lens that was fully extended to the 500mm position.  I was in Tv (shutter priority) mode and was shooting relatively slow (1/350ms) to get some blur in the prop.  The plane just almost filled the frame as it was, so there was very little cropping on it.  <br/> <br/>This air show was my first outing with my 10D  It had just come in two days prior and it is my first venture into the exciting world of DSLR, so I had a pretty big learning curve that day!  I had quite a few bad shots, but I walked away with a few decent ones too so overall I was pleased.  <br/> <br/>Thanks again everyone!<br/>Jason<br/></td>', 'Thanks everyone for the votes and kind comments left below... For those who asked, this was taken with me on the ground, and the plane was just about leveled off from a banked turn as it passed in front of me.  It was taken at Alliance Air Show in Fort Worth Texas, and the shot is of pilot Gene Soucy and his brave wing-walking accomplice, Teresa Stokes.  I had been panning with the plane through its turn and I let the camera track it with its AI Servo focus mode.  I was shooting handheld with a Sigma 50-500mm lens that was fully extended to the 500mm position.  I was in Tv (shutter priority) mode and was shooting relatively slow (1/350ms) to get some blur in the prop.  The plane just almost filled the frame as it was, so there was very little cropping on it.   This air show was my first outing with my 10D  It had just come in two days prior and it is my first venture into the exciting world of DSLR, so I had a pretty big learning curve that day!  I had quite a few bad shots, but I walked away with a few decent ones too so overall I was pleased.   Thanks again everyone!Jason', '2003-10-06 01:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(440044, 39802, 1717, '<td valign="top">beautiful, beautiful, beautiful!  congrats, soni! :hug</td>', 'beautiful, beautiful, beautiful!  congrats, soni! :hug', '2003-10-06 01:03:51.000000', NULL, 0),
